WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.080
In 2017, Netflix was knee-deep in superhero
projects.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.410
In addition to “MCU-sorta” properties
like Daredevil and Jessica Jones, they announced

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.490
a new set of comic series originating from
the Millarworld brand of comics — from world-famous

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.010
writer Mark Millar.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.470
While general audiences have seen some of
Millar's work receive live-action adaptations

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:26.860
before in the form of "Kingsman" and "Kick-Ass,"
these streaming series would explore a world

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.390
still unfamiliar to most.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.240
A new universe of possibilities kicked off
on May 7th, 2021, when the first of these

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.110
adaptations — "Jupiter's Legacy" — debuted
on Netflix.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.860
The new show exhibited precisely how it would
differentiate itself in a crowded market of

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.060
superhero properties with equal parts familial
drama and fight scenes.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.850
And that's not even mentioning the series'
dazzling cast, featuring the likes of Josh

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:59.110
Duhamel as the Utopian, Ben Daniels as Brainwave,
Leslie Bibb as Lady Liberty, Matt Lanter as

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.250
Skyfox, and more.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.610
Unfortunately, unlike the heroes at the center
of the show who can live well over a century,

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.800
"Jupiter's Legacy" has suffered an untimely
death.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.280
While the word "cancelation" may not have
come up explicitly, it's pretty clear that

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.930
Netflix plans on teleporting "Jupiter's Legacy"
Season 2 out of existence.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.970
On June 2nd, 2021, not even a month after
Season 1 debuted, Mark Millar himself broke

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.990
the news that season 2 wasn’t happening,
taking to Twitter to share an image of a statement

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:33.810
addressing the situation, plus some extra
commentary in the caption and in a follow-up

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:34.810
tweet.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:35.810
Millar said,

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.640
"I'm really proud of what the team achieved
with Jupiter's Legacy and the amazing work

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.030
everyone did on that origin season.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.890
I've been asked a lot about what we're planning
next with this world, and the answer is to

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.130
see what the super-villains are getting up
to.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.630
We've made the tough call of letting our incredible
cast out of their show commitment."

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.950
He noted in his statement that he's "confident
that [they'll] return to it later" — though

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.280
it's unclear who the “they” is.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.280
Netflix?

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.280
Millar and his team?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.390
Another streaming service?

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.310
Netflix tends to stay tight-lipped on its
shows' viewing numbers unless they're phenomenal.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:12.010
As such, the assumption is that "Jupiter's
Legacy" didn't do too well in that regard,

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.500
especially since the cast was let out of their
contracts entirely.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.830
The predominantly negative critical reviews
for "Jupiter's Legacy" could have played a

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.810
part in the demise of Season 2.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:27.170
Jupiter's Legacy" has a mere 38% critical
approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes, though

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.800
its audience score is more than double that,
sitting at 72%.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.670
There is no doubt that the show has a rabid
fan base, and Millar himself has a strong

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:40.380
following, so all this is a bit of a surprise
to have the axe fall so quickly.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.880
For the time being, the show's quick demise
is a sizable financial loss for Netflix.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.740
Borys Kit of the Hollywood Reporter mentioned
on Twitter that sources have suggested Jupiter's

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.660
Legacy Season 1 cost a reported $200 million
to make.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.710
Expensive plus bad reviews plus perhaps not
that large of an audience equals no season

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.710
two.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:04.380
Clearly, the financial aspect is critical
to all this, but on the bright side, in not

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.569
making another season of a show that might
have gotten the axe thereafter, Netflix isn't

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:10.660
pouring more money down the drain.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.350
Instead, money is being poured into a different
place.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.930
Some of the other Millarworld projects currently
in development at Netflix include "The Magic

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.140
Order," "American Jesus," and "Sharkey the
Bounty Hunter".

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:25.840
Hopefully, those don’t end up being a drain
on Netflix and their adventures into more

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.510
comic-based streaming shows.

